            <ArticleTitle>A quantitative approach to evaluating the effect of stimulating devices on the perception of noxious stimuli.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>205-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A new type of dolorimeter has been used in determining the nature of the mechanism responsible for the analgesic effect produced by electrostimulating devices. A study in normal subjects, yielding quantitative data on this analgesic effect, is reported.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
